<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  flashcard.entitlements — what lets a signed Foxy open an NFC session, and be
  opened by a card.

  Reading a card needs the NFC Tag Reading capability, which Apple gives only
  to a paid developer team: a free team cannot sign an app that claims it, and
  a build that claimed it would not install. So it is not in the project by
  default. project.yml reads the path from the environment:

      export FOXY_ENTITLEMENTS=tools/flashcard.entitlements     (in local.env)
      . ./local.env && xcodegen generate

  With it unset, Foxy builds and runs as before, and every card screen says
  NO CARD READER: the session is refused by the phone and the page is told so
  (CardLinkError.unavailable). The simulator needs none of this: it reaches a
  card over the Mac's loopback (Foxy/Flashcard/CardLink.swift).

  The second key is the associated domain a card's address opens Foxy through.
  A Foxy card answers as an NFC tag carrying one address, the same on every card,
  https://getfoxy.io/card. iOS reads it by itself with the screen on and shows a
  banner; the app associated with that address is the one a tap on the banner
  opens, and only a build signed with this entitlement is that app. Without it
  the same tap opens the page on the site in Safari. Associated Domains is a
  capability of a paid team too, so it lives in this file with the other and not
  in a build everyone can make. The site's association file names the app and
  the path /card; iOS reads it through Apple's servers when the app is installed,
  and a tap on the banner makes no request of its own. What the app does with
  the address is in Foxy/Flashcard/CardAddress.swift, and docs/CARD.md.

  The simulator's build (tools/simulator.entitlements) has no such key and could
  not use one: the association file names a team's app, and a simulator build is
  signed as no team, so the system would not hand it the address anyway.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.nfc.readersession.formats</key>
	<array>
		<string>TAG</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:getfoxy.io</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
